section: images
title: Images and registries
about: |
  The pack registries, the digests, the tags, and the images that the nodes pull.
rules:
- id: helm-digest-frozen
  title: The digest of a Helm chart in Palette names the bytes a cluster installs
  engines:
  - all
  tier: static
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  when: (.profiles | length) > 0
  what: |
    The sync of Palette keeps the first digest of a chart. This holds for a Helm registry and for
    an OCI registry of the provider type `helm`: the sync compares the annotations alone. A push
    again of the chart version changes what a new attach installs, and changes nothing that
    Palette shows. A running cluster keeps the old bytes, and a new attach gets the new ones. This
    rule names each such pack. The cloud check in `reproduce` compares the digest in the registry
    with the digest in Palette.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      [ .profiles[] | .source.name as $p | .packs[]
        | select(.type == "helm" or (.type == "oci" and (.registryProviderType // "") == "helm"))
        | "profile \($p): pack \(.name)@\(.version) is a chart of a \(if .type == "helm" then "Helm" else "OCI Helm" end) registry; Palette keeps its first digest, and a push again of \(.version) changes what a new attach installs" ]
  reproduce:
  - helm pull <chart> --version <version> --repo <url> && sha256sum <chart>-<version>.tgz
  - crane digest <oci host>/<chart>:<version>
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Compare the digest in the skip check of the sync for Helm and OCI Helm charts. A registry with immutable tags closes it at the source.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: a live run
    note: one profile version with one digest gave two different installs, before and after a push again
  - kind: source
    note: Helm, OCI Helm, and OCI Zarf compare the annotations alone; the other kinds compare the digest
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/helm-chart.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/addon-profile.json
- id: no-digest-kinds
  title: Each pack of the profiles carries a digest
  engines:
  - all
  tier: static
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  when: (.profiles | length) > 0
  what: |
    A Zarf package of an OCI registry, and a chart of a Helm registry with credentials, carry no
    digest in Palette. The record of such a pack has `hash.upstreamSource: none`, and a change of
    its bytes cannot show in a record or in `strata verify`. A manifest pack has no archive and is
    not counted.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      [ .profiles[] | .source.name as $p | .packs[]
        | select((.type // "spectro") != "manifest")
        | select((.hash.upstreamSource // "") == "none")
        | "profile \($p): pack \(.name)@\(.version) of type \(.type // "spectro")\(if (.registryProviderType // "") != "" then " (\(.registryProviderType) registry)" else "" end) has no digest in Palette; a change of its bytes cannot show" ]
  reproduce:
  - strata snapshot 'pack:<registry>/<name>@<version>' | jq '.packs[].hash.upstreamSource'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Give a digest to each pack kind. For a Zarf package, read the manifest digest of the registry; for a private Helm chart, read the chart archive.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: '#71, #75'
  - kind: run
    ref: a live run
  - kind: source
    note: the digest comes from the tag listing of the registry, and the listing of a Docker registry gives none
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/no-digest.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/addon-profile.json
- id: private-pack-registry-empty
  title: A private pack registry lists its packs
  engines:
  - all
  tier: palette
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  what: |
    A Spectro pack registry with `private: true` syncs as `Completed` in under a second, and
    Palette lists no pack of it. The same registry with `private: false` lists its packs at the
    next sync. Nothing in the status says that the sync read no pack. The world holds no registry
    document, so strata-preflight has no check; `strata packs` shows an empty registry.
  reproduce:
  - strata packs <pack> --registry <registry>
  - '{{ palette_curl }} "${PALETTE_API:-https://api.spectrocloud.com}/v1/registries/pack/summary" | jq ''.items[] | {name: .metadata.name, private: .spec.private, sync: .status.sync}'''
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Sync a private pack registry, or say in the sync status that a private registry lists no pack.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: a live run
  - kind: source
    note: Palette returns no pack of a private registry when it lists or reads packs
